WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.250
- [Instructor] We are told
a phone sells for $600

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:08.250
and loses 25% of its value per year.

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:12.550
Write a function that gives
the phone's value, V of t,

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:17.550
so value as a function of
time, t years after it is sold.

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.210
So pause this video, and have a go at that

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:22.480
before we work through it together.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.200
All right, so let's just
think about it a little bit.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.220
And I could even set up a table

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.870
to think about what is going on.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:32.910
So this is t, and this
is the value of our phone

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.990
as a function of t.

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:37.130
So it sells for $600.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:40.670
At time t equals zero, what is V of zero?

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:43.650
Well it's going to be equal to $600.

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:46.500
That's what it sells for
at time t equals zero.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:49.200
Now at t equals one,
what's going to happen?

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:52.090
Well it says that the phone loses 25%

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:53.600
of its value per year.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.270
Another way to rewrite that
it loses 25% of its value

00:00:57.270 --> 00:01:01.010
per year is that it retains, it retains,

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:04.130
100% minus 25% of its value per year,

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.980
or it retains 75%

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:11.980
of its value per year, per year.

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:16.480
So how much is it going to
be worth after one year?

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:19.617
Well it's going to be worth $600,

00:01:19.617 --> 00:01:24.160
$600 times 75%.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:25.550
Now what about year two?

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:28.151
Well it's going to be worth
what it was in year one

00:01:28.151 --> 00:01:30.670
times 75% again.

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:35.620
So it's going to be $600
times 75% times 75%.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:40.620
And so you could write
that as times 75% squared.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.830
And I think you see a pattern.

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:47.200
In general, if we have gone,
let's just call it t years,

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.890
well then the value of our phone,

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:52.210
if we're saying it in dollars,
is just going to be $600

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:54.575
times, and I could write it as a decimal,

00:01:54.575 --> 00:01:59.575
0.75, instead of 75%, to the t power.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:05.230
So V of t is going to be equal to 600

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:10.230
times 0.75 to the t power, and we're done.

00:02:11.363 --> 00:02:12.963
Let's do another example.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:17.320
So here, we are told that
a biologist has a sample

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:19.620
of 6,000 cells.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:22.650
The biologist introduces
a virus that kills 1/3

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.190
of the cells every week.

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:29.060
Write a function that gives
the number of cells remaining,

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:32.140
which would be C of t, the
cells as a function of time,

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:36.140
in the sample t weeks after
the virus is introduced.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.060
So again, pause this video

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:39.810
and see if you can figure that out.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:43.710
All right, so I'll set
up another table again.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:47.400
So this is time, it's in weeks,

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.200
and this is the number of cells, C.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.590
We could say it's a function of time.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:54.900
So time t equals zero, when
zero weeks have gone by,

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:56.510
we have 6,000 cells.

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:57.950
That's pretty clear.

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:00.140
Now after one week, how
many cells do we have?

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:01.750
What's C of one?

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:04.320
Well it says that the virus kills 1/3

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:07.030
of the cells every week,
which is another way of saying

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:09.692
that 2/3 of the cells are able to live

00:03:09.692 --> 00:03:11.580
for the next week.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:16.543
And so after one week, we're
going to have 6,000 times 2/3.

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:21.020
And then after two weeks,
or another week goes by,

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:22.920
we're gonna have 2/3 of
the number that we had

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:23.753
after one week.

00:03:23.753 --> 00:03:27.360
So we're gonna have 6,000
times 2/3 times 2/3,

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:30.630
or we could just write
that as 2/3 squared.

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:33.940
So once again, you are likely
seeing the pattern here.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:36.830
We are going to, at time t
equals zero, we have 6,000,

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:39.120
and then we're going to multiply by 2/3

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:42.440
however many weeks have gone by.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:45.710
So the cells as a function
of the weeks of t,

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:48.680
which is in weeks, is going
to be our original amount,

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:51.790
and then however many weeks have gone by,

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:55.140
we're going to multiply
by 2/3 that many times,

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:57.537
so times 2/3 to the t power.

00:03:57.537 --> 00:03:58.753
And we're done.

